This repository is licensed in two parts, because it contains two different
kinds of thing.

The protocol text is meant to be pasted into other people's configuration files.
Attaching an attribution requirement to a config snippet would be unenforceable
in practice and would discourage exactly the adoption the text exists for. So it
carries no conditions at all. The tooling that builds and tests that text is
ordinary software, and is licensed as such.

